//example - cards 

public class Main
{
	public static void main(String[] args) {
		int arr[]={2,1,3,4,6,5};
		
		
		//insertion sort
		for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++)
		{
		    int temp=arr[i];
		    int j=i-1;
		    while(j>-1 && temp<arr[j])
		    {
		        arr[j+1]=arr[j];
		        arr[j]=temp;
		        j--;
		    }
		}


Case	Time Complexity	Why?

Worst Case	- O(n²) ----	For i = n-1, do n-1 comparisons/shifts
Space	      - O(1)  ----	No extra arrays, just variables
		
		
		
	
